segments.translation:
With the third [verse]{pada} he speaks of purification. “[Mother-in-law]{sasu}” and so on: first of all, the [lord of yogis]{yogindra} makes the [vajra of body]{trivajra} firm by way of [deity yoga]{devatayoga}; through the [instruction]{upadesa} in [vajra recitation]{vajrajapa} he breaks the taking of [sides]{paksa} by the [moon]{moon} and the [sun]{surya}, and makes the [vajra of speech]{trivajra} [steady]{sthira}; and to make the [vajra of mind]{trivajra} firm he leads that [avadhūtī]{avadhuti} of the [joy of cessation]{viramananda}, merged into one with [innate joy]{sahajananda}, to the house of breath, the summit of [Sumeru]{pl-sumeru}. “[Key]{key}”: in sealing the [lock]{lock} shut, the door of the [root of the jewel]{manimula} is to be blocked; addressing himself so, he states the sequence himself. So the venerable [Kāṇha]{p-kanha} says:
“At the door of the [sky]{gagana}, where mind and [wind]{vayu} are, a firm [lock]{lock} is set;
if then, in the dreadful darkness, the jewel is made a lamp,
if the [sky]{gagana} touches upon the jewel of the Jina,
[Kāṇha]{p-kanha} says, while existence is enjoyed, [nirvāṇa]{nirvana} is accomplished.”
